  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nUpper trough moving through the Canadian prairies this morning, \nknocking down the ridge over Montana, and pushing a cold front \ninto the Dakotas.\n\nCooler temperatures along with gusty west to northeast winds are\nexpected across the region today. A Lake Wind Advisory has been\nissued for Fort Peck Lake for this afternoon. \n\nUpper ridge will rebound across the region through the remainder\nof the week with warming temperatures and dry conditions. \n\nBy the end of the week another upper trough will push across the\nwest coast, for another round of thunderstorms through the\nweekend.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nMade tweaks to PoPs early this morning and to winds for the Lake\nWind period. No other changes to NBM.",
